         ("Treat it as peritonitis and collect an effluent specimen for culture first", False, "The effluent is clear and there is no pain. The picture points to fluid passing through a defect in the diaphragm."),
         ("Ask her to lie flat to rest her breathing while waiting for the physician", False, "Breathlessness is worse lying down. She is kept upright while orders are awaited."),
         ("Report urgently, drain the abdomen, and keep her upright while awaiting orders", True, "Breathlessness worse lying down, low drain volumes, and a one-sided effusion suggest a leak into the chest. It is reported urgently, the abdomen is drained, and the patient is kept upright."),
